# Line-ending policy. This repo builds a Linux Docker image, so every file the
# image executes or parses MUST be LF on checkout — even on Windows.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true on Windows checks shell scripts out as CRLF,
# and `docker build` bakes a `#!/bin/bash\r` shebang into the image. The
# container then fails at start with "not found" / "bad interpreter: No such
# file or directory" (this broke v2.2.1 and every image built on Windows).
#
# The blobs are already stored LF; `eol=lf` makes the WORKING TREE match and
# overrides autocrlf regardless of a contributor's local git config.

*             text=auto eol=lf

# Deploy-critical: executed/parsed by Linux tooling — never CRLF.
*.sh          text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
*.conf        text eol=lf
Dockerfile    text eol=lf
*.py          text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalize.
*.gguf        binary
*.onnx        binary
*.docx        binary
*.png         binary
*.jpg         binary
*.jpeg        binary
*.ico         binary
